66. Concerning the Ambassador. 66
Once again he said to his disciples: 'Take heed and see,
{0} know in the manner that is being manifested forth to you — that there
are two great mysteries manifested forth in this sun which gives
light — in his shining-forth and in his setting. Look,
indeed, when he is to shine and be manifested forth in the cosmos until {1}
all the creatures of flesh — they draw themselves forth out of {2}
in which they exist, against the Radiance of the sun. Look,
again, at the evening, when the sun is to set forth from the cosmos:
all men of every place, together with all the (other) cattle,
are wont to go in into their hiding-places of darkness; the multi-
tude of the whole cosmos shut their mouths, and the night of darkness
comes upon them, and they go in, and they dwell within their
night of darkness in their hiding-places.
A great Raising-up is this mystery which is manifested forth in the sun.
For the time when the sun shall shine and {3} be manifested forth from the be-
ginning of the day — all men open their mouths, of {4}
